{"name":"Carol","hex":"#338dae","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Carol","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from the Germanic languages, popular in the middle of the 20th century."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male given name from the Germanic languages."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Carol"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carol (given name)","blocks":[{"text":"Carol is a unisex given name in English, although in contemporary usage it is more commonly used for women. It is a variant of the English Charles, Germanic Carl, and Latin Carolus. Spelling variations include Carroll, Caryl, and Carole."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carol_(given_name)","wikidata":"Q18201469"},{"title":"Avedon Carol","blocks":[{"text":"Avedon Carol is an American-born British feminist, anti-censorship, and civil liberties campaigner and a researcher in the field of sex crime, residing in England. She is a member of Feminists Against Censorship, and as part of their publishing group co-edited Bad Girls & Dirty Pictures (1993). She is the author of Nudes, Prudes and Attitudes (1994), and has also worked on other books by Feminists Against Censorship. On her own website, \"Avedon's Sideshow\", she publishes and compiles links to a wide array of stories and events."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Avedon_Carol_in_1979%2C_Arlington%2C_Virginia.jpg/330px-Avedon_Carol_in_1979%2C_Arlington%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avedon_Carol","wikidata":"Q4827971"},{"title":"Carol (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Carol is a 2015 historical romantic drama film directed by Todd Haynes. The screenplay by Phyllis Nagy is based on the 1952 romance novel The Price of Salt by Patricia Highsmith. The film stars Cate Blanchett, Rooney Mara, Sarah Paulson, Jake Lacy, and Kyle Chandler. Set in 1950s New York City, the story is about a forbidden affair between an aspiring female photographer and an older woman going through a difficult divorce."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Carol_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carol_(film)","wikidata":"Q15963780"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Cannes_2015_18.jpg/500px-Cannes_2015_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Cannes_2015_18.jpg/500px-Cannes_2015_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rooney Mara, Todd Haynes and Cate Blanchett during premiere of Carol at the 2015 Cannes Film Festival","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACannes_2015_18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cate_Blanchett_Deauville_2013_3.jpg/500px-Cate_Blanchett_Deauville_2013_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cate_Blanchett_Deauville_2013_3.jpg/500px-Cate_Blanchett_Deauville_2013_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACate_Blanchett_Deauville_2013_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Rooney_Mara_at_The_Discovery_premiere_during_day_2_of_the_2017_Sundance_Film_Festival_at_Eccles_Center_Theatre_on_January_20%2C_2017_in_Park_City%2C_Utah_%2832088061480%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Rooney_Mara_at_The_Discovery_premiere_during_day_2_of_the_2017_Sundance_Film_Festival_at_Eccles_Center_Theatre_on_January_20%2C_2017_i